{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the boys grew … and Esau became.</b> All the while they were small, they were not distinguishable in their deeds, and no one scrutinized them for what they were. Once they became thirteen years old, this one parted to the houses of study and this one parted to idolatry." "<b>Knows hunting.</b> To hunt and to deceive his father with his mouth — he would ask his father: Father, how does one tithe salt and how does one tithe soda? — for his father thought he was scrupulous in commandments (Tanchuma)." "<b>A man of the field.</b> As it sounds: an idle man who hunts beasts and birds with his bow." "<b>Wholehearted.</b> Not expert in all these things — his heart is as his mouth. One who is not sharp to deceive is called תָּם." "<b>Dwelt in tents.</b> The tent of Shem and the tent of Eber."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:31.161299074Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}